  "implementationAssessment": [
    "The whole-profile DOM path and its 16 MiB rejection are replaced by a bounded full JSON structural pass and independent pread cursors over the same verified descriptor.",
    "Only fixed-path spans and counts are indexed. The string table is a bounded enum bytearray. Marker columns are consumed in lockstep; all seven column lengths are verified before aggregation.",
    "The complete JSON document, including ignored values, must pass UTF-8, semantic duplicate-key, finite-number, syntax, truncation, trailing-data, depth, key, and array limits. JSON null remains distinct from cursor EOF and the undecoded sentinel.",
    "The ASCII small-value and array-prefix fast paths decode at most the current 64 KiB chunk with the same strict hooks and decoded-container limits. Incomplete or unsuitable prefixes fall back to the structural cursor; tracked child spans are retained.",
    "Counts and finished-marker observations are returned only after parsing, column consumption, descriptor/path identity, directory identity, profile listing, and the shared deadline checks all succeed. Unknown results retain null counts.",
    "The existing JSONL route and fixed completion-marker semantics remain. The collector never qualifies build success, an active compiler phase, remaining work, cache reuse, or a completion forecast."
  ],
